# Line-ending policy. 2026-07-26 audit finding 9.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with git's default `core.autocrlf=true`
# rewrites every text file to CRLF. `hooks/repo-integrity.mjs` then failed to
# read the frontmatter block of EVERY agent and skill, reporting all 38 roles
# and all 35 skills as malformed. Pinning LF here stops that happening to this
# repository; the readers in hooks/ are ALSO being made line-ending tolerant,
# because they parse the user's own project files too, and those may legitimately
# be CRLF on Windows. Both halves are needed — this file is not a substitute for
# tolerant parsing.
#
# 2026-07-26 further-pass audit fix: this used to claim "the CI job that
# deliberately builds a CRLF working tree overrides this after checkout" — no
# such job exists in .github/workflows/ci.yml, and never has. What actually
# tests the guard: hooks.test.mjs re-encodes a throwaway copy of this repo to
# CRLF and asserts repo-integrity.mjs still reports clean (see its `toCrlf()`
# helper), and the real `windows-latest` CI leg runs the whole suite on an
# actual Windows checkout — which is what caught the two genuine Windows-only
# bugs recorded in AUDIT-2026-07.md section 4.3. Corrected here rather than
# left as a stale claim nobody would otherwise notice.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch the bytes.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.vsix  binary

# Text, but pin the ones that break loudly if they arrive as CRLF.
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg  text eol=lf
